  body: "# Carer additional amount: named exclusions\n\n**Model-assisted source interpretation; unreviewed.
    No entitlement decision or executable rule.**\n\nThe captured paragraph describes a possible carer
    additional amount and names prisoners and people fully maintained by a religious order as exclusions.\n\
    \n## Evidence and scope\n\n[DMG 78100, PDF page 27](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e10327f5069cdc54868955/dmg-Ch-78.pdf#page=27)
    supports this scoped proposal. The source PDF SHA-256 is `d5e17de1d343fc6a6498089897b222a4989914fa53f85af9ddc8c9c05471e2b8`.\n\
    \nRead the qualifying conditions and DMG memos 12/23 and 01/26. This record is not a complete eligibility
    test or a current award decision.\n\nThe capture date, the publication page's update date and a date
    stated in the guidance have different meanings. Linked legislation and memos need their own provision,
    version and applicability review.\n\nMemo references are navigation to separately captured source
    evidence. They do not assert incorporation, supersession or current legal validity.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/carers
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The exclusions are stated in the paragraph about the additional amount for carers;
      retaining them prevents the broad carer concept being treated as unconditional entitlement.
    evidence:
    - page: page/78/0027
      quote: "78100 [See DMG memo 12/23] [See Memo DMG 01/26] When considering the amount of the AMG,
        an\n\nadditional amount for carers may be applicable 1. But the additional amount is not payable2
        in the case of\n\n\n1. prisoners and\n\n\n2. members of religious orders who are fully maintained
        by their order.\n\n\n                     1 SPC Act 02, s 2(3)(b) & (8); SPC Regs, reg 6(6)(a)
        & Sch I, para 4(1); 2 reg 6(2), (3) & (6)"
      locator: DMG 78100
